speechtext:
(/) deprive a person charged with a criminal offence of the right to be presumed innocent until proved guilty according to law in a fair and public hearing by an independent and impartial tribunal, or of the right to reasonable bail without just cause;
Mr. Speaker, I can see no way that this bill as it reads now can comply with the Canadian Bill of Rights.
This, Mr. Speaker, makes it a necessity to amend the bill, and I think the amendment I suggested is quite reasonable because it does not prevent identification but only the publication of information gathered by police officers. Its object is to force the court to destroy evidence after the case is heard and the individual is discharged.
